# IOS System Performance Optimization Guide

## 📊 Overview

This guide covers performance optimization strategies, tools, and best practices for IOS System.

**Performance Targets:**
- API Response Time (p95): <500ms
- API Response Time (p99): <1000ms
- Database Queries: <100ms
- Search Latency: <150ms
- Cache Hit Rate: >90%
- Throughput: >1000 req/s

---

## 🔍 Performance Analysis

### Database Analysis

**Run analysis script:**
```bash
python scripts/optimize/analyze_database.py
```

**Key metrics to review:**
- Slow queries (>100ms)
- Sequential scans on large tables
- Missing indexes
- Table bloat (dead tuples)
- Index usage statistics

**Example output:**
```
📊 SLOW QUERIES (Top 10)
1. Mean time: 250ms (calls: 1000, max: 500ms)
   SELECT * FROM documents WHERE title LIKE '%budget%'

💾 TABLE BLOAT
documents    | Size: 500MB | Dead: 50000 (10.0%) | ⚠️ NEEDS VACUUM

🔍 MISSING INDEXES (High Sequential Scans)
documents    | Seq scans: 10000 | Index usage: 20.0% | Size: 500MB
```

### Load Testing

**Using K6:**
```bash
# Baseline test
k6 run --vus 20 --duration 5m tests/load/k6-api-load-test.js

# Stress test
k6 run --stage 2m:50 --stage 5m:50 --stage 2m:100 tests/load/k6-api-load-test.js

# Spike test
k6 run --stage 10s:200 --stage 1m:200 --stage 10s:0 tests/load/k6-api-load-test.js
```

**Using Locust:**
```bash
# Web UI mode
locust -f tests/load/locust-load-test.py --host https://api.ios-system.com

# Headless mode
locust -f tests/load/locust-load-test.py \
    --headless \
    --users 100 \
    --spawn-rate 10 \
    --run-time 5m
```

